● TASK RESULT
Fixed WinBar layout and Advisor perspective per Step 4 review fix 2.
### Changes
- **WinBar.jsx**: Redesigned layout — user's team always on the left with their win % in their side's color, bar fills remaining width, opponent's % on the right. Parts legend on a second line labeled from the user's team's perspective with signed points (e.g. `team form −11.7 pts · draft +0.0 · side +14.1 · first pick +0.8`). Correctly maps `winProbability`'s P(blue wins) to the user's team regardless of side.
- **styles.css**: Updated WinBar CSS for new structure (`.win-bar-main`, `.win-bar-team`, single-fill track) and fixed media queries.
- **AdvisorPanel.jsx**: Always advises the user's team (first team select). Title shows team name ("Advisor · Cloud9 Kia"). Three modes: user's PICK turn → save/take/deny list (clickable); user's BAN turn → "Ban suggestions" from opponent's `likelyPicks` (clickable to ban); opponent's turn → "Your next pick" preview (non-clickable).
- **App.jsx**: Added `name` prop to `AdvisorPanel` so it can display the user's team name.
- **perspective.test.js**: New vitest test file verifying WinBar perspective logic (usPct mapping, parts sign flip on side swap, Elo symmetry).
### Verification
- `npx vitest run`: 37 tests passed (5 files, including new perspective.test.js)
- `npx vite build`: successful production build
- `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v`: 13 tests passed
